 "note": "Positive gain means the multiple-state receptor did better. Bootstrap unit is the homology component. Two CO-PRIMARY tests in stratum accept (followup_v1/PLAN.md, fixed before any 50-call pose existed): P1 on the rank-1 pose and P2 on the best of the top-5 distinct poses (>1 A apart). Each is decided on ci975_bonferroni, whose lower bound must exceed zero, keeping the family-wise error at 5%; ci95 is printed beside it for transparency and is not the decision rule. Everything else is secondary or exploratory and is reported whatever it shows. Oracle, top5 and success counts depend on the call budget, so they are never compared across the 8-call and 50-call runs."
